# WCAG 2.2 Accessibility Rules

When generating or modifying frontend code:

- Read `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/wcag.config.json` first. `standard` is `2.1` or `2.2`. `level` is `A`, `AA`, or `AAA`. The shipped file is WCAG 2.2 AA. A standard or level the user states in chat overrides the file for that request. If the file is missing or invalid, use WCAG 2.2 AA.
- When the resolved standard is **WCAG 2.1**, do not enforce 2.4.11, 2.4.12, 2.4.13, 2.5.7, 2.5.8, 3.2.6, 3.3.7, 3.3.8, or 3.3.9. 4.1.1 exists in 2.1 and was removed in 2.2; do not treat it as a practical HTML failure.
- Apply Level AAA criteria when the resolved level is AAA. The bullets below that cite a 2.2-only criterion apply only when the resolved standard is 2.2.
- Use semantic HTML first. Avoid ARIA unless necessary for custom widgets.
- Ensure keyboard operability and visible focus indicators (`:focus-visible`).
- Interactive targets must be at least 24×24 CSS pixels, unless the spacing or inline exception applies — SC 2.5.8. A link inside a sentence is exempt.
- Focused elements must not be entirely obscured by sticky headers, footers, or banners — use `scroll-padding` — SC 2.4.11.
- Provide single-pointer alternatives for any dragging interactions — SC 2.5.7.
- Authentication flows must support password managers and paste; avoid cognitive tests without alternatives — SC 3.3.8.
- Do not require re-entry of previously provided data in multi-step processes — SC 3.3.7.
- Help mechanisms (contact, chat, FAQ) must appear in consistent order across pages — SC 3.2.6.
- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (normal), UI components ≥ 3:1.
- Images need appropriate `alt` text; form controls need labels; page needs `lang`.
- 4.1.1 Parsing is obsolete in WCAG 2.2 — do not enforce it.

Refer to the `wcag-2.2` skill. WCAG 2.2 table: `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/references/wcag-2.2-success-criteria-table.md`. WCAG 2.1 table: `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/references/wcag-2.1-success-criteria-table.md`. Differences: `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/references/wcag-2.1-vs-2.2.md`. For deep audits, delegate to the `a11y-reviewer` subagent.